===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|hemlok}}, {{m|enm|hemeluc}}, from {{inh|en|ang|hymlīc}}, {{m|ang|hymlīce||hemlock, [[bryony]], [[convolvulus]]|lit=hops-like}}, from {{m|ang|hymele||hop-vine}}, from {{der|en|gem-pro|*humalaz}}, {{m|gem-pro|*humalōn}}, of unknown origin. Perhaps from {{der|en|xsc}}, from {{m|ira-pro|*háwmah||[[ephedra]]; juice}}, from {{der|en|iir-pro|*sáwmas}} from {{der|en|ine-pro|*sew-||to press out, extract}}.

{{rel-top|cognates}}
* {{qualifier|from Proto-Germanic *humalaz, *humalōn}} {{cog|non|humall}}, {{cog|gml|homele}}
* {{qualifier|from Sarmato-Scythian *haumala}} {{cog|os|хумӕллӕг||hops}}
* {{qualifier|from Sarmato-Scythian *hauma}} {{cog|ae|𐬵𐬀𐬊𐬨𐬀}}, {{cog|bal|tr=hum}}, {{cog|fa|هوم|tr=hōm}})
* {{qualifier|from Proto-Indo-Iranian *sauma}} {{cog|sa|सोम}})
More at [[suck]].
{{rel-bottom}}

